# AIStart360 Portal — Development Rules for Claude / Cursor

## Project Context
AIStart360.app — B2B SaaS Client Portal for AI-powered Business Diagnostics
Market: Kazakhstan/CIS, SME clients
Architecture: Multi-agent AI (HITL), RAG pipelines, Expert Review workflow

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 14 (App Router), TypeScript, React 18
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v3, shadcn/ui, Radix UI primitives
- **Database**: Supabase (PostgreSQL + pgvector), Prisma ORM
- **Auth**: NextAuth.js v5 beta + Supabase Auth
- **AI**: Vercel AI SDK (ai package) + @ai-sdk/anthropic + Claude API
- **State**: Zustand (client), TanStack Query (server state)
- **Forms**: react-hook-form + @hookform/resolvers + Zod
- **Deployment**: Vercel (stateless functions)
- **Orchestration**: n8n (external, port 5678)

## Architecture Rules
- **Multi-tenant by client_id** — all DB queries MUST include client isolation
- **Row Level Security** — always design with Supabase RLS in mind
- **Server Components by default** — use `'use client'` only when necessary
- **Never expose SERVICE_ROLE_KEY** to client-side code
- **Vercel functions are stateless** — no daemons, no persistent RAM/FS
- **Use `waitUntil`** for post-response work (logging, analytics)
- **AI calls via Vercel AI SDK** for streaming; direct @anthropic-ai/sdk for complex tool use

## File Structure
```
/app/(dashboard)/          — authenticated dashboard routes
/app/api/                  — API route handlers
/components/dashboard/     — feature-specific components
/components/ui/            — shared shadcn/ui components
/lib/                      — utilities, mock-data, navigation
/shared/api/               — client-side API service layer
/prisma/                   — schema, migrations, seed
```

## Naming Conventions
- Components: `PascalCase.tsx`
- Utilities: `camelCase.ts`
- API routes: `/app/api/[resource]/route.ts`
- DB queries: Server-only, via Supabase server client (`createServerClient`)
- Types: Suffix with `Type` or use Prisma generated types

## Code Quality Rules
- Always use **TypeScript types**, never `any`
- **Zod schema** for all form inputs and API request validation
- Prefer **server actions** over API routes for form mutations
- Use `cn()` helper for conditional Tailwind classes
- Always handle loading and error states in UI

## Document Processing Modules (installed)
- `pdf-parse` — parse client PDF uploads
- `mammoth` — extract text from .docx files  
- `xlsx` — parse Excel/financial statements
- `tesseract.js` — OCR for scanned documents
- `sharp` — image processing for thumbnails

## AI / Agent Modules (installed)
- `ai` + `@ai-sdk/anthropic` — main AI interface
- `@anthropic-ai/sdk` — direct Claude API for complex use
- `langfuse` — observability, trace every diagnostic run
- `@langchain/core` + `@langchain/textsplitters` — RAG text chunking

## Agentic Infrastructure
- **Skills Directory**: Located in `.agents/skills/`. Contains 1,300+ operational playbooks.
- **Research Reference**: `.agents/research/awesome-agents.md` summarizes leading agent frameworks.
- **Workflow Strategy**: Use the `@skill-name` notation or reference the `SKILL.md` files for complex operations like TDD, security audits, or architectural refactors.
- **Continuous Learning**: Before starting any new feature (e.g., GRI Diagnostic update), check for a relevant playbook in `.agents/skills`.

## Observability
- **Langfuse**: wrap every AI call with trace. Use client from `lib/langfuse.ts`
- Track: client_id, diagnostic_type, tokens_used, latency
- Self-hosted Langfuse runs at http://localhost:3002

## When generating code
1. Always check if a shadcn/ui component exists before creating custom UI
2. Use `react-hook-form` + `zod` for ALL forms — no uncontrolled inputs
3. For multi-step flows: use `@stepperize/react` or manual `useState`
4. File uploads: use `react-dropzone` with Supabase Storage
5. API errors: always return typed error responses with HTTP status codes
6. Never hardcode client data — use mock-data.ts patterns for dev, real DB for prod
